-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",155,{
[4929]="70010302\n1\tTalk to Throttólf\030Talk to Wethur\030Use Unlucky Dwarf\tThe four dwarves are somewhere inside the Brackwater, the cave up the slope east of Brogur. Brogur wants to know what happened to the four dwarves he sent to investigate the Brackwater, and has charged you with finding them.\n2\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is outside the cave known as the Brackwater, down the slope to its west. You have found the four dwarves Brogur sent into the Brackwater, and should report to him of their fates.\n",
[4930]="7001BEB2\n1\tRescue desperate soldier\030Rescue exhausted soldier\030Rescue wounded soldier\tThe Elf-soldiers may be found among the trees of the Mirk-eaves. Agorin has asked you to aid the missing Elves should you find them amongst the forests of the Mirk-eaves.\n2\tTalk to Agorin at Echad Sirion\tAgorin is at Echad Sirion on the eastern banks of the Anduin. You should return to Agorin and let her know that you have found and aided the missing soldiers.\n",
[4931]="70010303\n1\tCollect Half-orc Orders\030Collect Map of Hollin\030Collect Threatening Missive\030Collect List of Promises\030Collect Partial Report\tInformation about the half-orcs can be found at their camp-fires inside the cave Filgogân, south-west of Bósi's camp, across the dried-up Sirannon. Símbi has asked you to obtain information from each of the half-orc camp-fires inside the cave Filgogân.\n2\tBring information on the half-orcs to Símbi\tSímbi is outside the cave Filgogân, south-west of Bósi's camp, across the dried-up Sirannon. You have gathered a great deal of information about the half-orcs in Filgogân and should bring it all to Símbi.\n",
[4932]="7001BEE7\n1\tCollect bandages (total: 5)\tThe supplies are at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin. Agorin has tasked you with finding clean bandages that have been misplaced among the rest of the military supplies that were hastily brought across the Anduin.\n2\tThe wounded Elves are at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin. Now that you have collected enough bandages, you should see to the treatment of the Elf-soldiers who were seriously wounded during the first wave of the assault upon Mirkwood.\t\n3\tTalk to Agorin at Echad Sirion\tAgorin is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin\n",
[4933]="70010304\n1\tCollect Painted Stone (total: 6)\tHalf-orcs inside the cave of Filgogân, south-west of Bósi's camp and across the dried-up Sirannon, surely carry some proof of their loyalty to Graug's master. Símbi has asked you to ascertain the common thread that binds these half-orcs together, and bring evidence of it to him.\n2\tBring painted stones to Símbi\tSímbi is outside the entrance to the cave Filgogân, south-west of Bósi's camp, across the dried-up Sirannon. You have recovered stones, crudely painted with the emblem of a hand, from many of the half-orcs within Filgogân, and should bring them now to Símbi.\n",
[4934]="70010305\n1\tFind the strongbox at the top of the waterfall\tThe treasure of which Ógur spoke may be at the top of the waterfall deep within the cavern known as the Brackwater. Throttólf has asked you to find the passages leading to the top of the waterfall so you can investigate the possibility that some treasure might be found there.\n2\tTalk to Throttólf\tThrottólf is in the cave called the Brackwater, near the entrance, down a passage from the base of the waterfall. You found the strongbox at the top of the waterfall, but whatever treasure it might once have contained has long since fallen into dust. You should return to Throttólf with these tidings.\n",
[4935]="70010306\n1\tUse Pile of Skulls\tPiles of bones can be found throughout the cave of Filgogân, and Lofrík's gold tooth might be among them. Trausti has asked you to search the bone piles within the cave for the distinctive gold tooth of his friend Lofrík.\n2\tBring chipped gold tooth to Trausti\tTrausti is somewhere within the cave of Filgogân. You have found Lofrík's distinctive gold tooth, and should return to Trausti with the sad tidings of his friend's death.\n",
[4936]="70010307\n1\tDefeat half-orcs in Filgogân (total: 8)\030Defeat Graug\tThe cavern Filgogân is south-west of Sandar, across the dry river-bed of the Sirannon, in the south-western corner of the surrounding hills. Sandar has asked you to defeat the half-orcs that have encamped inside Filgogân, as well as their leader Graug.\n2\tTalk to Sandar\tSandar is at the small dwarf encampment north-east of Filgogân, with Bósi. You have thinned the ranks of the half-orcs in Filgogân and defeated their leader Graug, and should now return now to Sandar.\n",
[4937]="7005B184\n1\tIgnite barrels of sapper-bombs at Zaghúth\tBarrels of sapper-bombs can be found at Zaghúth. You should ignite barrels of sapper-bombs at Zaghúth.\n2\tIgnite barrels of sapper-bombs at Zaghúth (total: 10)\tBarrels of sapper-bombs can be found at Zaghúth. You should ignite barrels of sapper-bombs at Zaghúth.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have ignited many barrels of sapper-bombs at Zaghúth.\n",
[4938]="7006AE96\n1\tExplore the south-western chamber\030Explore the south-eastern chamber\030Explore the north-eastern chamber\030Explore the north-western chamber\tGhâr Mejet is a vile place within the underground. Explore its chambers and report on your findings.\n2\tExplore the main chamber\tThe main chamber of Ghâr Mejet is the vilest place in the area. Explore its chambers and report on your findings.\n3\tTalk to Yâshri outside of Ghâr Mejet\tInform Yâshri of your findings.\n",
[4939]="7005A662\n1\tExplore Brúvraum\tBrúvraum can be found north-west of Maergrind. You should explore Brúvraum for Varthmath.\n2\tDefeat gredbyg at Brúvraum (total: 8)\030Collect grodbog hive samples (total: 8)\tBrúvraum can be found north-west of Maergrind. You should defeat gredbyg and collect samples from the hive.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated gredbyg and collected grodbog hive samples.\n",
[4940]="7005A676\n1\tTalk to Varthmath at Zidir-nesad\tVarthmath can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset, in Máttugard. You should talk to Varthmath at Zidir-nesad.\n2\tTravel to Ronglagam\tRonglagam can be found south-east of Zidir-nesad in Máttugard. You should travel to Ronglagam.\n3\tDefeat stone-claws at Ronglagam (total: 10)\030Collect bones (total: 8)\030Collect dirt samples (total: 6)\tRonglagam can be found south-east of Zidir-nesad in Máttugard. You should defeat stone-claws and collect samples at Ronglagam.\n4\tBring the samples to Varthmath near Ronglagam\tVarthmath can be found near Ronglagam in Máttugard. You should bring the samples to Varthmath.\n",
[4941]="7003301F\n1\tExplore the kitchens of Uzbad-bakân\030Explore the Orc-housing at Uzbad-bakân\030Explore the forge at Uzbad-bakân\030Explore the armoury at Uzbad-bakân\tUzbad-bakân can be found south of the Hall of Flowing Water. You should head south through Zelem-melek and explore Uzbad-bakân, the stronghold of the Orcs in Zelem-melek.\n2\tTell Foreman Mögr of the presence of many Orcs in Zelem-melek\tForeman Mögr can be found in the Twenty-first Hall. You have explored the massive Orc-encampment of Uzbad-bakân, and found their foothold to be very strong. You should convey this information to Mögr at once.\n",
[4942]="7005A663\n1\tExplore Vâr Nuchur\tVâr Nuchur can be found west of Maergrind. You should explore Vâr Nuchur for Varthmath.\n2\tDefeat gredbyg at Vâr Nuchur (total: 8)\030Collect grodbog hive samples (total: 8)\tVâr Nuchur can be found west of Maergrind. You should defeat gredbyg and collect samples from the hive.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated gredbyg and collected grodbog hive samples.\n",
[4943]="7002FE47\n1\tFind the Hale-gap\tIt is not a bad idea to gather food and water while you can, for the thought of being lost in the woods without such necessities is a gruesome one.\n2\tCollect wild turnips (total: 5)\030Collect clean drinking-water (total: 5)\tTurnips and fresh water can be found along the Entwash River in the Hale-gap. You should collect fresh water and edible plants while they are still available, for you do believe these necessities will not be readily found within Fangorn.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected ample water and food, should it come in handy while in this wild place. It may be long before you look upon another market-vendor.\n",
[4944]="70030CE4\n1\tExplore the ancient tomb\tThe ancient tomb lies to the south of Elthengels, hidden in a remote corner of the Norcrofts by a waterfall. The ancient tomb awaits your exploration.\n2\tExplore the depths of the ancient tomb\tThe ancient tomb lies to the south of Elthengels, hidden in a remote corner of the Norcrofts by a waterfall. The ancient tomb awaits your exploration.\n",
[4945]="70032D6A\n1\tBegin your exploration of Zelem-melek by claiming the Wide Halls (total: 2)\tThe Wide Halls are at the bottom of the Great Hall of Durin. You should begin your exploration of Zelem-melek in the Wide Halls.\n2\tHead west and begin your exploration of Zelem-melek\tThe greater passages of Zelem-melek can be found by heading west along the lower hall. You should head west from where you planted the banners.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have begun your exploration of Zelem-melek.\n",
[4946]="7005AB0F\n1\tDestroy drake nests (total: 9)\tMolkha has given you a satchel of explosive containers to quickly destroy the many cliff-top drake nests. You should destroy drake nests in Flogalith with Molkha's bombs. The sloping path to Flogalith is to the north-west of Molkha's position.\n2\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tYou have destroyed many drake nests in Flogalith. You should return to Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.\n",
[4947]="70071CD5\n1\tPick up barrels of black powder (total: 5)\tPick up barrels of black powder and destroy goblin catapults in Glúkroz. Glúkroz can be found north-east of Sen Chatâk.\n2\tSet alight catapults with black powder (total: 5)\tSet alight black powder near catapults within Glúkroz.\n3\tReturn to Elder Jangâli in Sen Chatâk\tReturn to Elder Jangâli in Sen Chatâk.\n",
[4948]="7005B22F\n1\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should talk to Shúkurz and see if he will agree to Múta's plan.\n2\tRetrieve supplies in Aslíf\tShúkurz has asked you to take fresh supplies to a supply drop. You should take some supplies from the supply area of Aslíf.\n3\tDeliver supplies\tYou have retrieved fresh supplies to deliver. You should find the drop point in front of some gates at the top level of the 'Abad-nuhbu, to the east.\n4\tWhistle at the supply drop\tYou have delivered the supplies at the specified location. Shúkurz also asked you to whistle after dropping off the supplies.\n5\tTalk to Shúkurz in Aslíf\tYou have delivered the supplies and done everything Shúkurz asked of you. You should return to Aslíf on the upper tier and talk to him if he's returned.\n",
[4949]="7001B677\n1\tExtermination of Gorogrod\t\n",
[4950]="70039AE0\n1\tLook for something to carry water in\tFire threatens to consume this building if it is not extinguished soon. You should look for something to use near the water to put the flames out.\n2\tFind something to carry water in\tFire threatens to consume this building if it is not extinguished soon. You should look for something to use near the water to put the flames out.\n3\tThrow the bucket of water onto the flames of the burning building\tThe burning building is in the lumber-yard, north-east of Aldburg. You should bring the bucket full of water back to the burning building and extinguish the flames.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have successfully extinguished the flames of the burning building.\n",
[4951]="70030DBE\n1\tTalk to Sigeric\tSigeric is in the prison of Snowbourn. Gísling wants you to interrogate Sigeric and see if he is willing to part with any information about who sent him to undermine Snowbourn.\n2\tStare Sigeric down and see if he talks\tSigeric is in the prison of Snowbourn. Perhaps if you stare Sigeric down, he will break.\n3\tShake your fist at Sigeric\tSigeric can be found inside the prison of Snowbourn. Sigeric refuses to cooperate with the people of Snowbourn and has now mocked your attempts to break his will. Perhaps you should take a more threatening approach.\n4\tTalk to Sigeric\tSigeric can be found inside the prison of Snowbourn. You should talk to Sigeric.\n5\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling can be found in central Snowbourn. You should report Sigeric's refusal to cooperate to Gísling.\n6\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Sigeric has proven to be a brutal traitor of Rohan, and Gísling wishes for you to tell Fastred of Sigeric's threats against the Sutcrofts.\n",
[4952]="7002EF1D\n1\tDefeat uruks at Thornhope (total: 6)\tUruks can be found within the ruins of Thornhope in the Entwash Vale. You should defeat as many uruks as possible to help satiate Béortnoth's thirst for vengeance.\n",
[4953]="70026738\n1\tTalk to Adadhrond at Echad Garthadir\tEchad Garthadir lies some distance from the Way of Kings, within Annúminas. The Rangers have sent you to lend aid to Echad Garthadir.\n",
[4954]="70072F02\n1\tTravel ahead of Isamó to the sloping path that leads out of Starkhaven\tThe sloping path that leads out of Starkhaven is to the south. You should travel ahead of Isamó and ensure the way is clear for her to follow.\n2\tClimb north-west to the gate out of Starkhaven\tA path out of Starkhaven climbs to the north-west. Isamó asked that you clear the way to that gate for her.\n3\tTalk to Isamó by the gate\tIsamó has arrived at one of the paths that leads out of Starkhaven.\n",
[4955]="70045263\n1\tDefeat Variag scouts (total: 12)\tDefeat some of the Variag scouts who linger outside the walls of Ost Rimmon.\n2\tTalk to Glánhar\tYou should tell Lady Glánhar that you have defeated a number of scouts outside of Ost Rimmon.\n",
[4956]="7002FD44\n1\tDefeat crebain (total: 10)\030Bait traps for crebain (total: 8)\tThe crebain and traps can be found to the south-west of Garsfeld. Gísil wants you to defeat the crebain that have flocked around Garsfeld and bait traps outside the town to ensnare the foul birds.\n2\tTalk to Gísil at the Mead Hall of Garsfeld\tGísil can be found in the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. You should return to Gísil and let him know that you have done as he directed.\n",
[4957]="7003A48C\n1\tDefeat Uruk-hai sentries (0/6)\tThe eyes and ears of Madh-fushaum, the Uruk-hai sentry in the watchtowers around the outer wall are entrusted with the safety of the entire army.\n2\tDefeat Uruk-hai sentries (total: 6)\tThe eyes and ears of Madh-fushaum, the Uruk-hai sentry in the watch-towers around the outer wall are entrusted with the safety of the entire army.\n3\tComplete\tThe Uruk-hai sentries were battle-hardened warriors and a crucial aspect of the White Hand army. Removing them struck a blow to the safety and coordination of the forces within Madh-fushaum.\n",
[4958]="7004A8CB\n1\tFind the source of Shelob's brood in the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tThe source of the spiders can be found somewhere within the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Legolas has asked you to find the source of Shelob's brood in the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have found the source of the spiders in Cirith Ungol: the Under-gate.\n",
[4959]="7006BB28\n1\tReach the Utug-bûr scouting location\tReach the Utug-bûr scouting location that Neshurga described.\n2\tScout out Utug-bûr to gather information\tScout Utug-bûr from the location that Neshurga described.\n3\tReturn to Neshurga in Ub Nishir\tReturn to Neshurga in Ub Nishir with the information you've gathered on Utug-bûr.\n",
[4960]="700395D3\n1\tTravel to Bosa's Farm\tBosa's Farm can be found to the east of Middlemead in northern Kingstead. Thane Mágla has asked you to seek out Egbalth in hopes of aiding him in exposing the agent of Wormtongue in Middlemead.\n2\tSearch for any sign of Egbalth\tBosa's Farm can be found in northern Kingstead. You have arrived at Bosa's Farm to find it overrun by the White Hand. You should search the farm for any signs of life.\n3\tExamine Egbalth\tEgbalth can be found near one of the burned houses at Bosa's Farm in northern Kingstead. You have spotted a fallen soldier of Middlemead. You should investigate if this is the man Mágla meant for you to meet.\n",
})
